    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75749" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐγγία</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐγκία</span></b> , ἡ, Lat. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>uncia</i>, as adopted by the
			Sicil. Greeks, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				510
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.789
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>in Top.</u>
				210.7
			</span></i>:—written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀγκία</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				203
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sophr.
				151
			</span></i>: hence Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐγκιαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i>of
				one uncia</i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1042.23
			</span></i> (Sunium, <span class="entity">ii/iii A. D.</span>): <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐγκιασμός</span></b> , ὁ,
				<i>measurement by unciae</i>, in pl., <i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nov.</u>
				107.1
			</span></i>.</div>
